WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.982
A running total uses an ordered window frame.

00:00:02.982 --> 00:00:08.382
The calculation starts at the beginning of the partition and ends at the current row.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:12.187
As the current row moves forward, the frame grows.

00:00:12.187 --> 00:00:17.292
If we partition by department, each department gets its own running total.

00:00:17.292 --> 00:00:21.327
Running and moving calculations depend on the window frame.

00:00:21.327 --> 00:00:28.602
Defaults can be surprising, especially with duplicate ordering values or LAST_VALUE.

00:00:28.602 --> 00:00:33.082
Write the frame explicitly when the intended range matters.

00:00:33.082 --> 00:00:38.548
A clear frame makes the query easier to audit and protects against subtle changes in data.
